I have a dataset with 3 species and I want to test whether the allometry pattern is similar or different between them. For that, I did a test of homogeneity of slopes:

reg <- procD.allometry(coords~Csize,~species,groups=~species,slope=~Csize,iter=1999,logsz=FALSE, print.progress=FALSE,data=gdf_C1)

Here I obtain that my 3 species show different slopes (null hypothesis of parallel slopes rejected).

Then, I try to calculate the angle between these slopes using the following function:

advanced.procD.lm(coords ~ Csize,~Csize*species,groups=~species,angle.type = "deg",slope =~Csize, iter=999,data=gdf_C1)

However, when I run this analysis, there is no result related to the angles between slopes vectors in my output (although there are other outputs such as slopes, effect sizes, etc) Am I missing something?

Thank you very much in advance.

All the best,

Nicole

